Claude 101 — Day 11: Use Cases for Claude

Overview

Today I completed the eleventh lesson of Anthropic’s Claude 101 course.

This lesson focused on practical ways to use Claude in different professional roles and industries. I learned how Claude can help streamline everyday work, from analyzing data and creating reports to preparing for sales meetings and organizing research.

What I Learned

Claude can be applied to many different professional workflows, including:

* Project management
* Data analysis
* Sales
* Marketing
* Finance
* HR
* Legal
* Research

The key is to identify repetitive, time-consuming, or complex tasks where AI can provide useful support.

General Professional Use

Some examples that can be applied across different roles:

* Generate project status reports.
* Analyze patterns in user feedback.
* Create reusable Skills based on brand guidelines.

Sales

Claude can help sales teams:

* Build competitive battle cards.
* Research prospects before meetings.
* Create sales reports from pipeline data.

Marketing

Claude can help marketers:

* Analyze campaign performance.
* Repurpose content for different platforms and audiences.
* Extract insights from marketing data.

Finance

Claude can support finance workflows by:

* Building financial models.
* Drafting investment memos.
* Understanding and extending complex spreadsheets.

HR

Claude can help HR teams:

* Create onboarding guides.
* Develop documentation for different roles.
* Improve the employee onboarding experience.

Legal

Claude can assist with:

* Tracking complex discovery timelines.
* Organizing legal documents.
* Identifying patterns in large amounts of information.

Research

Claude can support researchers by:

* Planning literature reviews.
* Organizing academic sources.
* Verifying statistics and calculations from raw data.

Key Takeaways

* Claude can be useful across many different professions.
* AI becomes more valuable when integrated into real workflows.
* The best use cases often involve repetitive, complex, or time-consuming tasks.
* Use Case Galleries can provide inspiration for applying Claude to specific roles.
* Understanding use cases helps move from simply “using AI” to solving real problems with AI.

My Potential Use Cases

As someone learning software development and AI, I can use Claude for:

* Java and Spring Boot code reviews.
* Debugging and explaining code.
* Creating technical documentation.
* Generating GitHub README files.
* Researching new technologies.
* Preparing for technical interviews.
* Analyzing and improving my learning workflow.

Reflection

Today’s lesson helped me think beyond simply asking Claude questions.

The real value of AI comes from identifying specific tasks where Claude can save time, improve quality, or help me work more effectively. I want to continue experimenting with different use cases and find workflows where AI can become a practical part of my daily learning and development.

